\begin{frame}{One-Time Pad}
The one-time pad combines each message bit with an independent random key bit.
\begin{itemize}
\item Security is information-theoretic when the key is truly random.
\item Keys must never be reused across two different messages.
\end{itemize}
\begin{frame}{Diffie--Hellman Key Exchange}
Two parties agree on a shared secret over a public channel.
\begin{itemize}
\item Security rests on the hardness of the discrete logarithm problem.
\end{itemize}
\end{frame}
\end{document}

